WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.699
OK, let's jump into audience questions for
the week.

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:07.859
The first is, hey, David, how likely is violence
after the November election?

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:14.440
So there's a few different aspects to this
question that you're not clarifying violence

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.280
against or by which group.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.860
And I think there's a few different scenarios
that could lead to violence.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:28.500
Now, the most likely scenario that leads to
violence is Trump claims it was rigged and

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.860
his supporters take to the streets with guns.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:38.769
That would be the top like red alert violence
possibility in my mind.

00:00:38.769 --> 00:00:47.239
Are there scenarios in which so, you know,
there are right wingers who seem to be suggesting

00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:55.399
that if Trump gets reelected, the left is
going to become so out of control, furious

00:00:55.399 --> 00:01:01.609
that the left will start rioting and burning
things to the ground and looting and and and

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:05.019
all of this stuff.

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:07.090
That's not really what I'm afraid of.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:14.070
I think that if Donald Trump were to get reelected,
there will be it'll sort of be a 50/50 effect.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:20.010
Some people, much like when Trump was first
elected in November of 2016, will be outraged

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.840
and will take to the streets.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.820
And as you remember, from November of 2016,
those were widely peaceful protests.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.180
November, December 26.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:35.369
I don't even remember incidents, you know,
nationwide protests, hundreds and hundreds

00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:36.479
of thousands of people protesting.

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:40.420
And, you know, you could try find some news
story of some anecdote, but it was not part

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:41.420
of the narrative.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:45.550
Very different than the narrative that the
right created around the George Floyd protests.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:49.999
So some people on the left, certainly if Trump
is reelected, they will be out there protesting.

00:01:49.999 --> 00:01:53.570
But there's also going to be a lot of people
on the left who were just totally deflated.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:59.080
And I expect a portion of the left will check
out of politics for maybe not for years, but

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.590
certainly until the 2022 midterm.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:06.179
And then we'll get involved in the 2024 election
relatively late because it will be.

00:02:06.179 --> 00:02:11.830
I mean, listen, I understand I've said before,
Trump is better for my business, but he's

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.130
terrible for the country.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:16.440
And so I am fine with my business not doing
as well.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:21.430
If it's good for the country, but if it's
another four years of Trump, it is good.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.420
I'm going to certainly be deflated.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.710
And I know there are lots of people on the
left who will be as well.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:29.350
And I would not be shocked for a bunch of
those people to check out.

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:33.300
So I don't believe there's a real risk of
violence if Trump wins.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:38.980
Now, if Trump loses, there's a couple different
scenarios there as Trump loses by an insane

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:43.120
margin, like electorally, it's a huge margin
and popular vote.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:47.820
I don't think that the right is likely to
become too violent in that case.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:53.180
Trump could claim it's obviously rigged because
I never would have lost by this much.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:56.940
But I think the truth is that if both the
popular vote and the electoral vote are big

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:03.650
margins for Biden, I think that by and large,
the Trump ists will just say, wow, we just

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:04.650
lost.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.610
And they will essentially disappear for some
period of time.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.430
I don't think they're likely to be violent
in that case.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:17.730
I think the two scenarios for violence would
be big popular vote win, but it's really tight

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.320
electorally.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:24.450
And Trump loses by just like one or two states
and claims it's wrecked.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:27.470
I think that scenario could certainly lead
to violence.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:31.860
And then I think the one that is most likely
to lead to Trump is out in the streets.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:37.980
Is that everything is close and Trump loses
both electorally and popular vote and says

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.050
it was rigged.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:43.130
And that's the one where I would worry about,
you know, the so-called gun people that Donald

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:49.850
Trump has referred to going out there and
doing some some some horrible things.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:57.820
I believe it will be relatively short lived
if and when it becomes clear that Trump just

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:04.240
lost and no secretary of state is going to
save him and that even if he could file some

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:09.400
lawsuit to get a recount or even flip one
state, that that it won't be enough in the

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:14.190
scenario where it's a bigger victory for Joe
Biden, if indeed that happens.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:21.130
I think that the violence will be quelled
relatively quickly and by inauguration time,

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.190
I believe it will essentially be over.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:30.220
Now, whether we see more radical extremists
activated if Trump is removed.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:33.400
That's a fair question, which I'd have to
think about a little more.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:38.350
But I think that the most likely scenario
for violence is a Trump loss.

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:41.750
That is not a major loss, that it's close.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:47.510
And Trump claims it's rigged, maybe refuses
to concede and continues to argue that either

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.060
vote by mail went wrong or something like
that.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:54.160
That's the scenario that to me lends itself
most to violence in the streets.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.511
And I hope that authorities will be ready
and prepared to.

00:04:58.511 --> 00:04:58.530
With that.

